    "created_at": "2021-05-08T18:44:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-08T18:44:40Z",
    "body": "NetBSD does not support `LONG_BIT` sysconf. It doesn't even seem to be POSIX.\r\nA way which would work on NetBSD (supposing a C compiler is available):\r\n```c\r\n#include <stdio.h>\r\nint main() {\r\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", (int)sizeof(void*));\r\n    return 0;\r\n}\r\n```\r\nWhich would return either 64 or 32.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
