    "created_at": "2021-06-24T11:53:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-08T08:28:07Z",
    "body": "This is just an FYI for those looking to run Starship on NetBSD - I've created a [pkgsrc-wip](https://pkgsrc.org/wip/) package for it (look in [starship/](https://wip.pkgsrc.org/cgi-bin/gitweb.cgi?p=pkgsrc-wip.git;a=tree;f=starship;hb=HEAD)). The package currently builds and installs fine from pkgsrc but only on platforms *other than NetBSD* due to a few issues, but those are being worked on.\r\n\r\nIn particular, we've identified the following as blockers:\r\n* ~libc crate doesn't support `waitid()` ([libc #2243](https://github.com/rust-lang/libc/issues/2243))~ **resolved**\r\n* rust-battery crate doesn't support NetBSD ([rust-battery #20](https://github.com/svartalf/rust-battery/issues/20)) - workaround in place to not build the battery module on NetBSD\r\n* ~libc crate doesn't include `si_status()` in siginfo_t ([libc #2265](https://github.com/rust-lang/libc/issues/2265))~ **resolved**\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
